26::
0:
Operator
1:
%s missing\n
Tool %s is not used in\n
current program.\n
Maybe because it has been deleted or\n
it is not defined.\n
\t\n
Change to another tool using the\n
Jogging window.
2:
%s missing\n
Wobj %s is not used in\n
current program.\n
Maybe because it has been deleted or\n
it is not defined.\n
\t\n
Change to another workobject using\n
the Jogging window.
3:
Directory not created!\n
The directory %s cannot be created.\n
Probably, because directory already\n
exists or the disk is write-protected.\n
\t\n
Check if directory exists or if disk\n
is write-protected.\n
Check also if space on disk is enough.
4:
Robot Hold confusion!\n
The used tool and the used work object\n
cannot both, in the same time, be hold\n
by robot or be stationary.\n
\t\n
Check the robhold component of the\n
used tool and work object.
5:
%s missing!\n
The workobject %s contains\n
a coordinated mechanical unit which\n
cannot be found.\n
\t\n
Check the mechanical unit component of\n
the workobject.
6:
%s Userframe!\n
The workobject %s contains\n
a coordinated mechanical unit which\n
has no defined userframe.\n
\t\n
Check the mechanical unit component of\n
the workobject.
7:
Jogging not permitted!\n
Jogging cannot be done in this mode.\n
\t\n
Release the joystick and enabling\n
device and repeat.\n
Check also active mechanical unit.
8:
Tool mass undefined!\n
Jogging cannot be done if the used tool\n
has an undefined mass\n
\t\n
Enter a value for the mass, into the\n
tooldata for the used tool.
9:
Unsynchronized robot!\n
The robot or external axis are\n
unsynchronized.\n
\t\n
Synchronize robot or external axis.
10:
Orientation error!\n
Orientation in %s is unnormalized.\n
\t\n
Check orientation value.
11:
Parameter faults!\n
Loading of parameters in\n
%s\n
cannot be fulfilled.\n
For reason, see\n
%s\n
\t\n
Copy the file\n
%s\n
to a floppy and examine reasons\n
using an ordinary text editor!
12:
No Parameters loaded!\n
There are no parameters in\n
%s\n
\t\n
Check the file\n
%s\n
using an ordinary text editor!
13:
Jogging not permitted!\n
Jogging of mechanical unit is\n
not possible.\n
Unit is not activated.\n
\t\n
Activate the mechanical unit.
14:
Disk is full!\n
No info is saved in Change Log about\n
the parameter change because no space\n
available on disk.\n
\t\n
Try to delete files or\n
reorganize your disk.
15:
PP cannot be set!\n
PP cannot be set to routine\n 
'%s' because it has parameters.\n
\t\n
Make a routine which call '%s' or\n
remove the parameters.
16:
PP cannot be set!\n
PP cannot be set to routine\n 
'%s' because it resides in a\n
module which has NOSTEPIN as\n
module attribute.\n
\t\n
Copy the routine '%s' to\n
another module or change the\n
module attribute.
17:
PGM_TELLBACK code %d\n
\t\n
No more information available.
18:
RAPID syntax error!\n
The program cannot be loaded because of\n
syntactical error(s).\n
\t\n
A RAPID syntax check program for the PC\n
or QuickTeach can be used to detect the\n
error(s). The file PGMCPL1.LOG on the\n
internal RAM disk contains information\n
about the error(s).
19:
Data input error!\n
The component '%s' in data\n
type '%s' is not correct.\n
The limits are\n
%s!\n
\t\n
Check data and enter the correct\n
value.
20:
PP cannot be set!\n
PP cannot be set to routine\n 
'%s' because it is defined as\n
a trap routine.\n
\t\n
Change the definition for the\n
routine '%s'\n 
to 'Procedure'.
21:
Cannot show items!\n
The number of selected items exceeds the\n
current memory limit specified for this\n
configuration. The items can thus not\n
be shown.\n
\t\n
Reduce the number of data or\n
change the configuration to a memory\n
board with more memory.
22:
Cannot show all items!\n
Only %d variables (out of %d) will be\n
listed.\n
All variables cannot be shown because\n
the current memory limit specified for\n
this configuration will be exceeded.\n
\t\n
Reduce the number of data or\n
change the configuration to a memory\n
board with more memory.
